# BuildKit reads this in preference to a .dockerignore at the context root,
# which is what lets the ignore rules live in this repository while the context
# is the workspace directory above it.

# Version control history. The build passes its version in with -ldflags
# because copying a repository's history to learn one string is not a trade
# worth making.
**/.git
**/.github

# Build outputs, which would only invalidate the cache.
#
# The binary patterns are anchored one level down — */pacenote-server, matching
# <repo>/pacenote-server — and not **/pacenote-server. The ** form also matches
# server/cmd/pacenote-server, which is a directory and is the package this image
# is built from: the build then fails with "directory not found" on a path that
# is plainly there in the checkout.
**/dist
**/bin
*/pacenote-server
*/pacenote-server.exe
**/*.test
**/*.out
**/*.prof

# A running server's data directory, and anything else local.
**/pacenote-data
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/node_modules
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/.DS_Store

# The client repository, if it is checked out in the same workspace. Nothing in
# this image comes from it.
telemetry

# The workspace file is written by the build, not copied.
go.work
go.work.sum
